      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Upload journey 1 user(s) — everyday file">
        <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">The FULL upload journey — initiate, multipart POST to the CDP Uploader, then
validate — as one closed loop per user, so the report shows what an upload
costs END TO END, where the validate-only staircase isolates the service&apos;s
own cost. Each iteration is a real new upload of the committed everyday
fixture (journeyFile), so the uploader and its virus scanner are inside the
measurement.

There is no client-side scan poll: the backend&apos;s validate route waits for
the scan itself (waitForUploadReady), so the &quot;validate+scan&quot; leg carries the
scan wait — the same wall-clock a user at the frontend experiences, without
a polling loop&apos;s noise in the report.</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${__P(journeyUsers1,1)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">1</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">${__P(journeyStepDurationSeconds,30)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.delay">${__P(journeyDelay1,395)}</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.same_user_on_next_iteration">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
